  "notes": [
    "The separator report of DWSIM swaps the labels of the mass flows: 0.0215854 kg/s belongs to the liquid (crude methanol, 0.677542 mol/s of mostly methanol) and 0.0104565 kg/s to the vapor (recycle gas). The stream table is consistent and is what is stored in 'streams'.",
    "Molar enthalpy and entropy of the DWSIM stream table are sensible values. The energy flow includes the formation enthalpy (as H_total_mix in thermo-sim does), so duties and energy flows are compared directly.",
    "The tutorial text says the recycle gas has H2/CO = 2.0. DWSIM gives 0.663615/0.330657 = 2.007: CO is slightly more soluble in the liquid than H2.",
    "The equilibrium reactor expression is evaluated on fugacities relative to 1 atm according to the tutorial text. Whether P_ref is 1.0 or 1.01325 bar matters here (delta nu = -2); the tests compare both against the DWSIM extent.",
